# Lenovo Yoga Book 9 13IRU8: let the "iio" group stream the two gyroscopes.
#
# A hinge angle integrated from the gyroscopes (one per half) needs their
# buffered 100 Hz stream with timestamps, and by default that is root-only:
# /dev/iio:deviceN is 0600 and the buffer and scan_elements switches are 0644
# root. This opens exactly those to one group, so the daemon can run as an
# ordinary user service.
#
# Matched by name, never by number: iio:deviceN is enumeration order and
# differs between units (here the gyros are device1 and device3; the
# accelerometer and light sensor that iio-sensor-proxy holds are 0 and 2).
#
# Setup, once:
#   sudo groupadd --system iio && sudo usermod -aG iio "$USER"
#   sudo install -Dm644 70-yoga-gyro-access.rules /etc/udev/rules.d/
#   sudo udevadm control --reload
#   sudo udevadm trigger --action=add --subsystem-match=iio --attr-match=name=gyro_3d
# then log out and back in for the group to apply.
#
# Note: any member of the group can read the machine's rotation. On a
# single-user laptop that is you; do not add other accounts casually.

SUBSYSTEM=="iio", KERNEL=="iio:device*", ATTR{name}=="gyro_3d", GROUP="iio", MODE="0660", \
  RUN+="/bin/sh -c 'cd /sys%p && chgrp iio buffer/enable buffer/length buffer/watermark scan_elements/*_en in_anglvel_sampling_frequency && chmod g+w buffer/enable buffer/length buffer/watermark scan_elements/*_en in_anglvel_sampling_frequency'"
